From: mift2609 <rolex>
Subject: [PATCH] net: wwan: qcom_bam_dmux: register netdev when channel reopened

The modem may send OPEN for a channel the driver already considers open
(e.g. after a modem restart or when the AP re-opens the data port). The
driver then only logged "Channel already open" and returned, so a netdev
that was never registered stayed missing and the data call could never be
brought up. Do the same work as a fresh open in that path.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate (device/firmware workaround)
---
--- a/drivers/net/wwan/qcom_bam_dmux.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wwan/qcom_bam_dmux.c
@@ -545,6 +545,15 @@
 
 	if (__test_and_set_bit(hdr->ch, dmux->remote_channels)) {
 		dev_warn(dmux->dev, "Channel already open: %u\n", hdr->ch);
+		/*
+		 * The netdev may not exist yet although the channel is marked as open
+		 * (e.g. after a modem restart or when the AP re-opens the data port).
+		 * Without it there is no data path at all, so make sure it exists.
+		 */
+		if (netdev)
+			netif_device_attach(netdev);
+		else
+			schedule_work(&dmux->register_netdev_work);
 		return;
 	}
 
